Fix the GC stack walker on aarch64. The runtime assumed the saved
link register sits in the topmost slot of every ML frame and that the
C primitives' frame record is at the top of their frame; neither holds
with LLVM/GCC on AArch64, so the collector read garbage return
addresses and aborted in sml_lookup_frametable.

- smlsharp_gc plugin (LLVM >= 20): record each function's LR spill
  slot from its callee-saved info and emit it in the frame table.
- runtime: walk frames with that per-function offset, locate the
  caller frame with the CFA, and record the top frame's code address
  when a stack range is closed (bl leaves it only in x30).

